Breaks: btrfs-snapman (<< 0.7.0)
Replaces: btrfs-snapman (<< 0.7.0)
Description: btrfs subvolume snapshot manager - root helpers and config
 btrfs-snapman creates, lists and deletes btrfs snapshots of selected
 subvolumes, with one snapshot folder per subvolume. It does not use Snapper
 and does not impose a layout.
 .
 This package holds the parts both front ends share: three small root
 helpers that do all privileged work, the configuration in /etc/btrfs-snapman
 and the shared Python modules. The helpers only accept volume names from
 root-owned configuration, plus folders the administrator approves as new
 volume locations. Install btrfs-snapman (GTK) or btrfs-snapman-cli
 (terminal) to use them.

Package: btrfs-snapman
Architecture: all
Depends: btrfs-snapman-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
         gir1.2-adw-1,
         pkexec,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: btrfs subvolume snapshot manager - GTK4 interface
 btrfs-snapman creates, lists and deletes btrfs snapshots of selected
 subvolumes, with one snapshot folder per subvolume. It does not use Snapper
 and does not impose a layout.
 .
 This package is the libadwaita GUI. It runs as the user; every operation
 goes through pkexec to one of the root helpers in btrfs-snapman-common,
 each with its own polkit action.

Package: btrfs-snapman-cli
Architecture: all
Depends: btrfs-snapman-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3,
         sudo,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: btrfs subvolume snapshot manager - terminal interface
 btrfs-snapman creates, lists and deletes btrfs snapshots of selected
 subvolumes, with one snapshot folder per subvolume. It does not use Snapper
 and does not impose a layout.
 .
 This package is btrfs-snapman-cli: a full-screen curses interface and
 scriptable subcommands, for SSH sessions and headless machines. It needs no
 GTK or polkit; it reaches the root helpers in btrfs-snapman-common through
 sudo, or directly when run as root (e.g. from cron).
